  "_about": "The site manifest: site block, external links, and the categories with their titles and their guides in display order. Everything about one guide (codename, labels, llms.txt line, related guides, freshness rows) is in its own meta.json (_tools/articles/<slug>/ for generated guides, _tools/handmade/<slug>/ for the rest). python3 _tools/build-site.py writes pages.json, the guide lists in index.html, llms.txt, related.json, _tools/freshness.json, search.json and sitemap.xml from these; never edit those by hand. In \"guides\": a string is a guide slug, {\"planned\": {en, ru}} is a SOON row, {\"external_links\": true} is where the \"external\" links are listed on the index page, {\"also\": slug} lists a guide a second time on the index page only (its home category is the one that names it as a plain string).",
